(with feces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clinical Course and Symptoms: Features a gradual stepladder fever climbing daily,) Tj
T*
(constitutional headache, dry cough, malaise, relative bradycardia \(Faget's sign\),) Tj
T*
(abdominal discomfort, splenomegaly, and characteristic 'rose spots' on the trunk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Diagnosis and Clinical Care: Confirmed via blood cultures, bone marrow cultures,) Tj
T*
(or rapid serological assays. Treatment necessitates culture-guided antibiotic) Tj
T*
(therapy \(such as azithromycin, ceftriaxone, or fluoroquinolones\), safe drinking) Tj
T*
(water practices, and adequate nutritional support.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Complications: Life-threatening complications such as intestinal hemorrhage or) Tj
T*
(ileal perforation typically manifest during the third week of untreated illness.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
