(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) Tj
T*
(POLYCYSTIC OVARY SYNDROME \(PCOS\) AND ENDOCRINE HEALTH) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reproductive Endocrinology, Hyperandrogenism & Insulin Resistance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition: PCOS is a common heterogeneous endocrine disorder affecting 6 to 15%) Tj
T*
(of reproductive-aged women, defined by the Rotterdam criteria \(at least two of:) Tj
T*
(ovulatory dysfunction/irregular cycles, biochemical or clinical hyperandrogenism,) Tj
T*
(and polycystic ovarian morphology on ultrasound\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pathophysiology and Symptoms: Underlying pathophysiology centers on insulin) Tj
T*
(resistance, hyperinsulinemia, and ovarian theca-cell androgen hypersecretion.) Tj
T*
(Manifestations include oligomenorrhea, hirsutism \(excessive facial/body hair\),) Tj
T*
(severe cystic acne, androgenic alopecia, and central weight gain.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Multimodal Clinical Management: First-line therapy focuses on lifestyle) Tj
T*
(modification \(low-glycemic nutritional diet, regular aerobic and resistance) Tj
T*
(exercise\) to enhance insulin sensitivity. Pharmacotherapy includes combined oral) Tj
T*
(contraceptive pills for cycle regulation and androgen suppression, and metformin) Tj
T*
(for metabolic stabilization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
