(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) Tj
T*
(ACUTE GASTROENTERITIS, FOOD POISONING AND REHYDRATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Gastroenterology, Enteric Pathogens & Electrolyte Homeostasis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition: Acute gastroenteritis is sudden mucosal inflammation of the stomach) Tj
T*
(and intestines caused by foodborne bacterial toxins \(Staphylococcus aureus,) Tj
T*
(Bacillus cereus\), bacterial pathogens \(Campylobacter, Salmonella\), or enteric) Tj
T*
(viruses \(Norovirus, Rotavirus\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pathophysiology and Symptoms: Presents with acute nausea, projectile vomiting,) Tj
T*
(watery diarrhea, diffuse cramping abdominal pain, low-grade fever, and dehydration) Tj
T*
(due to rapid intestinal fluid and electrolyte secretion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rehydration Therapy and Care: The cornerstone of management is continuous oral) Tj
T*
(rehydration therapy using WHO-formulated oral rehydration salts \(ORS\), sipped) Tj
T*
(slowly in small quantities. Avoid anti-motility drugs \(like loperamide\) during) Tj
T*
(acute infectious diarrhea, and avoid dairy, fatty, or caffeinated items until) Tj
T*
(normal stool consistency returns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Emergency Warning Signs: Seek immediate emergency intravenous care for severe) Tj
T*
(dehydration \(sunken eyes, dizziness on standing, absence of urination for over 8) Tj
T*
(hours\), high fever, inability to tolerate oral sips, or bloody stools \(dysentery\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
