(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) Tj
T*
(CHRONIC FATIGUE, ACADEMIC BURNOUT & NEUROENDOCRINE STRESS ADAPTATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Behavioral Medicine, Neuroendocrinology & Cortisol Homeostasis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition: Burnout and chronic stress-related exhaustion represent a state of) Tj
T*
(profound emotional, physical, and cognitive depletion resulting from chronic,) Tj
T*
(unmitigated occupational or academic stressors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pathophysiology and Systems Impact: Prolonged stress hyperactivates the) Tj
T*
(hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal \(HPA\) axis, leading to chronically dysregulated) Tj
T*
(cortisol secretion, autonomic nervous exhaustion, impaired prefrontal cognitive) Tj
T*
(processing, and down-regulated immune responsiveness.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Holistic Recovery and Boundary Setting: Sustainable recovery requires structural) Tj
T*
(boundary setting \(limiting screen hours, dedicated study disconnect periods\),) Tj
T*
(physiological restorative sleep \(8 hours consolidated sleep\), progressive somatic) Tj
T*
(relaxation, restorative nutritional meals, and cognitive reframing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clinical Referral: Persistent fatigue exceeding six months unresponsive to rest) Tj
T*
(requires clinical workup to rule out chronic fatigue syndrome \(ME/CFS\), occult) Tj
T*
(anemia, hypothyroidism, or major depressive disorder.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
